    <http://example.org/node/chunk1> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Public Tender - Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) Implementation of an AI assistance solution for hospital staff 1. Context and objectives The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) is a public regional hospital serving the Belval region (approximately 1,200 beds and 4,500 staff across medical, care and medico-administrative functions). As part of The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) digital transformation and of the national Ségur du numérique en santé programme, The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) wishes to improve the efficiency of The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) staff and the quality and safety of the care delivered to patients. Staff face a growing complexity of procedures, a multiplicity of information sources (care protocols, recommendations from the Haute Autorité de Santé (HAS), internal procedures, regulatory texts, business systems) and an increasing volume of administrative and documentation work that reduces the time available for patient care. In this context, The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) wishes to procure, deploy and operate an artificial intelligence solution that assists staff in staff daily activities - facilitating access to information, improving the quality of written outputs, and reducing processing and documentation times - while remaining strictly a non-decisional support tool." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk10> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Change-management support and staff training are expected. 10. Evaluation criteria Offers will be evaluated against the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution; compliance with regulatory requirements; level of security; data sovereignty; quality of integration with the existing SIH/DPI; total cost of the proposed solution; consideration of environmental issues; capacity for innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk11> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Public Tender - Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) Implementation of an AI assistance solution for hospital staff 1. Context and objectives The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) is a public regional hospital serving the Belval region (approximately 1,200 beds and 4,500 staff across medical, care and medico-administrative functions). As part of The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) digital transformation and of the national Ségur du numérique en santé programme, The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) wishes to improve the efficiency of The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) staff and the quality and safety of the care delivered to patients. Staff face a growing complexity of procedures, a multiplicity of information sources (care protocols, recommendations from the Haute Autorité de Santé (HAS), internal procedures, regulatory texts, business systems) and an increasing volume of administrative and documentation work that reduces the time available for patient care. In this context, The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) wishes to procure, deploy and operate an artificial intelligence solution that assists staff in staff daily activities - facilitating access to information, improving the quality of written outputs, and reducing processing and documentation times - while remaining strictly a non-decisional support tool." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk12> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The present contract covers the design, implementation and deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution must provide hospital staff with an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from hospital staff work environment, capable of supporting hospital staff in hospital staff clinical-administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of supporting them in their clinical-administrative activities may notably cover: retrieval of information from internal procedures, care protocols and applicable regulation; assistance in drafting medical and administrative documents; support in handling dossiers (admissions, coding, medico-social pathways, etc.); support for the continuity of care between professionals, shifts and services. The solution must fit into the existing practices of staff and must not introduce a rupture in clinical or administrative workflows. 3. Functional scope 3.1 Information consultation assistance. The solution must let staff quickly access reliable, up-to-date information drawn from the authority's internal procedures, care protocols and HAS recommendations, applicable regulatory texts, and internal documents (guides, notes, reference frameworks, drug references)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk13> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must contextualise The solution answers to the staff member's request. 3.2 Drafting assistance. The solution must assist the drafting of clinical and administrative content, notably discharge summaries and medical reports (comptes-rendus), medical correspondence and patient letters, administrative documents and dossier syntheses. Generated content must be adapted to the clinical/administrative context and conform to expected quality standards. 3.3 Dossier-handling assistance. The solution must assist staff in analysing and handling dossiers by surfacing relevant information, recalling applicable rules, and suggesting actions or verifications. The solution must support medical coding (PMSI / ICD-10) for activity reporting (T2A)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk14> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must take the dossier context into account where available. No decision may be automated. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of care. The solution must facilitate the continuity of care between professionals and services by enabling relevant information sharing, an understanding of the context of an in-progress patient pathway, and an efficient resumption of handling by another professional. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints 4.1 Personal and health data protection. The titleholder must guarantee strict compliance with the GDPR." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk15> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Health data is processed as special-category data (GDPR Art. 9) and medical confidentiality (secret médical) must be preserved. Data must be hosted exclusively within the European Union; no transfer of data outside the European Union is authorised; sensitive data must be appropriately protected (encryption, pseudonymisation where relevant). 4.2 Health-data hosting (HDS). The infrastructure hosting The solution must hold the French Hébergeur de Données de Santé (HDS) certification. 4.3 Explainability and traceability. Recommendations or suggestions produced by The solution must be explainable. It must be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements that led to an output (source grounding, audit trail), consistent with HAS guidance on the use of AI in healthcare. 4.4 Medical responsibility." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk16> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must be designed as an assistance tool. No clinical or medico-administrative decision may be automated without explicit validation by a qualified professional. The solution must be positioned so as not to require medical-device qualification (CE marking / MDR); should any use case approach medical-device qualification (CE marking / MDR), the bidder must explicitly address the implications. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance. The solution must provide response times compatible with daily clinical use." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk17> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As an indication, a response time below 2 seconds is expected for common queries. A high level of answer relevance is expected. 5.2 Availability. Continuity of care requires a high level of availability, including outside office hours (24/7 services). An availability target of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration and interoperability. The solution must integrate with the existing hospital information system (SIH) and the electronic patient record (DPI)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk18> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must support health interoperability standards (HL7 / FHIR), the national health identifier (INS), and the national framework (Ségur du numérique en santé, Mon espace santé / DMP). API-type interfaces are expected, as is integration with user directories. 6. Sovereignty constraints the authority's attaches particular importance to data sovereignty. Hosting must be performed on SecNumCloud-qualified infrastructure or equivalent, and particular attention will be paid to dependency on non-European suppliers. 7. Budget constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 900,000 over 5 years." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk19> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The annual operating cost must remain controlled and compatible with the authority's budgetary capacity. The titleholder must propose an approach that optimises costs while guaranteeing the expected quality of service. 8. Environmental constraints As part of the authority's sustainable-development policy, the authority's wishes to limit the environmental footprint of the authority's information systems. The titleholder must propose a solution that contributes to reducing energy consumption and relies, as far as possible, on low-carbon infrastructure. 9. Deployment terms the project must be conducted progressively, with a pilot phase on a limited perimeter (one or two departments) followed by progressive generalisation to all services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk2> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The present contract covers the design, implementation and deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution must provide hospital staff with an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from hospital staff work environment, capable of supporting hospital staff in hospital staff clinical-administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of supporting them in their clinical-administrative activities may notably cover: retrieval of information from internal procedures, care protocols and applicable regulation; assistance in drafting medical and administrative documents; support in handling dossiers (admissions, coding, medico-social pathways, etc.); support for the continuity of care between professionals, shifts and services. The solution must fit into the existing practices of staff and must not introduce a rupture in clinical or administrative workflows. 3. Functional scope 3.1 Information consultation assistance. The solution must let staff quickly access reliable, up-to-date information drawn from the authority's internal procedures, care protocols and HAS recommendations, applicable regulatory texts, and internal documents (guides, notes, reference frameworks, drug references)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk20> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Change-management support and staff training are expected. 10. Evaluation criteria Offers will be evaluated against the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution; compliance with regulatory requirements; level of security; data sovereignty; quality of integration with the existing SIH/DPI; total cost of the proposed solution; consideration of environmental issues; capacity for innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk21> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires a solution that improves efficiency, quality and safety of care delivered to patients, facilitates access to information, reduces processing and documentation times, and provides intelligent assistance tools. The project must be conducted progressively with a pilot phase on a limited perimeter followed by progressive generalisation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk22> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our company's PM methodologies and past public sector references, what is the proposed project plan and timeline for delivering this solution? Based on our company's hybrid delivery model combining agile iterations with a phase-gate structure suited to public and health procurement, our company's propose a project plan that aligns with the client's requirements. our company's approach consists of five phases: Framing, Design, Pilot, Generalisation, and Run." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk23> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In Framing, our company's will work closely with the client to define the project scope, objectives, and deliverables. Framing will last approximately 2-3 months." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk24> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The Design phase will focus on designing this solution, including the development of the intelligent assistance tool and integration with existing hospital information systems. The Design phase is expected to take around 4-5 months." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk25> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Pilot will involve deploying this solution on a limited perimeter, testing, and validating this solution effectiveness. our company's anticipate Pilot to last about 3-4 months. Following the successful completion of Pilot, our company's will proceed with Generalisationire hospital." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk26> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Generalisation is expected to take around 6-8 months. Finally, in Run, our company's will ensure the smooth operation of this solution, provide maintenance and support, and continue to monitor and improve this solution performance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk27> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Run will commence after Generalisation and will continue for an extended period. our company's past public sector references, such as the regional council and mutual health insurer projects, demonstrate our company's ability to deliver similar solutions within a 9-12 month timeframe. Considering the scope and complexity of The project, our company's estimate the overall duration to be around 18-24 months. our company's believe that our company's proposed project plan and timeline align with the client's requirements for progressive implementation and phased delivery. our company's agile approach will enable our company's to adapt to changing requirements and ensure that this solution meets the client's needs and expectations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk28> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires a solution that provides response times below 2 seconds, integrates with existing hospital information systems and electronic patient records, supports health interoperability standards, and has API-type interfaces. The solution must also be hosted on SecNumCloud-qualified infrastructure or equivalent, with particular attention to dependency on non-European suppliers." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk29> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For each of these requirements, state whether each of these requirements is FULLY COVERED, PARTIALLY COVERED or NOT COVERED by our current technology stack, and describe the proposed architecture. The client's requirement for response times below 2 seconds is PARTIALLY COVERED by our current technology stack. our platform's median latency is 1.3 seconds, and common single-document queries are below 2 seconds at p95." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk3> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must contextualise The solution answers to the staff member's request. 3.2 Drafting assistance. The solution must assist the drafting of clinical and administrative content, notably discharge summaries and medical reports (comptes-rendus), medical correspondence and patient letters, administrative documents and dossier syntheses. Generated content must be adapted to the clinical/administrative context and conform to expected quality standards. 3.3 Dossier-handling assistance. The solution must assist staff in analysing and handling dossiers by surfacing relevant information, recalling applicable rules, and suggesting actions or verifications. The solution must support medical coding (PMSI / ICD-10) for activity reporting (T2A)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk30> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, complex multi-source synthesis queries may reach up to 2.5 seconds at p95, which does not fully meet The client's requirement for response times below 2 seconds. The client's requirement for integration with existing hospital information systems and electronic patient records is FULLY COVERED by our current technology stack." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk31> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our platform's has standard connectors and custom adapters for SIH/DPI integration, as well as a framework alignment with Ségur / Mon espace santé–DMP, and our partner with Ligeo Santé for health interoperability. The client's requirement for support of health interoperability standards is FULLY COVERED by our current technology stack." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk32> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our platform's supports health interoperability standards such as HL7 and FHIR, with a production-grade FHIR-HL7 connector for the main resources and extended resource coverage on the roadmap. The client's requirement for API-type interfaces is FULLY COVERED by our current technology stack." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk33> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our platform's has an API-first design, with documented APIs (REST + webhook) that can be embedded in existing work environments. The client's requirement for hosting on SecNumCloud-qualified infrastructure or equivalent is PARTIALLY COVERED by our current technology stack. our offer a sovereign HDS tier hosted on OuraneCloud, which is SecNumCloud-qualified, but our do not have information on whether a sovereign HDS tier hosted on OuraneCloud, which is SecNumCloud-qualified is equivalent to other SecNumCloud-qualified options." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk34> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client's requirement for particular attention to dependency on non-European suppliers is PARTIALLY COVERED by our current technology stack. our offer a sovereign European open-weight model hosted by Faber IA on OuraneCloud, which reduces dependency on non-European suppliers, but our also have the option of using top-tier proprietary models accessed via API, some of which are operated by non-European providers. The proposed architecture would involve deploying Our platform's on the sovereign HDS tier hosted on OuraneCloud, utilizing our standard connectors and custom adapters for SIH/DPI integration, and supporting health interoperability standards through our FHIR-HL7 connector. our would also provide API-type interfaces for easy integration with existing hospital information systems and electronic patient records." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk35> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To address the response time requirement, our could explore optimizing Our platform's configuration or scaling up our infrastructure to ensure that complex multi-source synthesis queries can be completed within the 2-second threshold." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk36> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires strict GDPR compliance, including hosting data exclusively within the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union, encryption and pseudonymisation of sensitive data where relevant. The solution must also provide explainability and traceability of outputs, consistent with HAS guidance on the use of AI in healthcare." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk37> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What security controls and regulatory compliance measures will we implement to meet these requirements? To meet The client requirements for strict GDPR compliance and other specified needs, we will implement several security controls and regulatory compliance measures." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk38> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Firstly, as we hosting partner is OuraneCloud, which is a SecNumCloud-qualified sovereign cloud, we can ensure that data is hosted exclusively within the European Union. hosted aligns with The client requirement for data sovereignty and no transfer of data outside the European Union. For encryption, we utilize TLS 1.3 for data in transit and AES-256 for data at rest, ensuring that sensitive data is protected." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk39> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, we use of pseudonymisation further enhances the protection of sensitive information. we also adhere to strict key management practices through we the European Union-based infrastructure, adding another layer of security for sensitive data. In terms of explainability and traceability, we product Atelier supports explainability and traceability, providing grounded-in-sources explanations and retrieval traces. supports is consistent with HAS guidance on AI in healthcare, particularly aspects like explainability, human oversight, and source traceability." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk4> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must take the dossier context into account where available. No decision may be automated. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of care. The solution must facilitate the continuity of care between professionals and services by enabling relevant information sharing, an understanding of the context of an in-progress patient pathway, and an efficient resumption of handling by another professional. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints 4.1 Personal and health data protection. The titleholder must guarantee strict compliance with the GDPR." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk40> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Moreover, being ISO 27001 certified since 2023 for the scope of Development, delivery, and operations, and having the ISO 27701 certification as an extension for privacy information management, demonstrates we commitment to robust security and data protection practices. The HDS certification held through OuraneCloud, which is a SecNumCloud-qualified sovereign cloud hosting infrastructure further ensures compliance with health-data hosting regulations. we data protection measures include tenant isolation, ensuring strict separation between client corpora and logical separation per engagement." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk41> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Role-based access control (RBAC), audit logging of access and system outputs, and the appointment of a Data Protection Officer (DPO) are also part of we comprehensive approach to security and compliance. For regulatory experience, particularly with GDPR delivery in healthcare contexts including special-category health data, we has experience working with public-sector and health clients. we familiarity with frameworks such as CNIL guidance, HDS reference framework, and HAS guidance on AI in healthcare ensures we are well-equipped to navigate the complex regulatory landscape of healthcare technology." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk42> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Lastly, we control mapping links platform features directly to applicable obligations, ensuring that audit evidence is readily available when needed. By implementing several security controls and regulatory compliance measures, we demonstrates we capability to meet The client stringent requirements for GDPR compliance, data security, and explainability in the use of AI within healthcare contexts." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk43> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires that no clinical or medico-administrative decision may be automated without explicit validation by a qualified professional." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk44> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must also be positioned so as not to require medical-device qualification (CE marking / MDR)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk45> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What legal risks should we flag, and are we compliant with the regulatory requirements for this project? we should flag the legal risks associated with medical-device qualification and the automation of clinical or medico-administrative decisions. we Legal function is responsible for monitoring obligations related to the EU AI Act requirements for AI systems used in a health context, as well as GDPR, medical confidentiality, and HDS framework." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk46> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Where a use case could approach the medical-device threshold, Our company's Legal function will flag the CE/MDR implications and the consequences for liability and positioning. flag ensures that we are aware of the potential risks and can take necessary steps to mitigate the potential risks." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk47> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As for compliance with regulatory requirements, we maintains regulatory compliance with the help of we Security & Compliance function, particularly in the context of health deployment. we monitor obligations related to GDPR, including Art. 9 special-category data and Art. 28 processing agreements, medical confidentiality, HDS framework, and EU AI Act requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk48> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, I do not have information on whether we specific solution or services are designed to avoid requiring medical-device qualification or if our specific solution or services inherently prevent the automation of clinical or medico-administrative decisions without explicit validation by a qualified professional." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk49> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Therefore, further review and consultation with relevant departments would be necessary to confirm compliance with these specific regulatory requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk5> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Health data is processed as special-category data (GDPR Art. 9) and medical confidentiality (secret médical) must be preserved. Data must be hosted exclusively within the European Union; no transfer of data outside the European Union is authorised; sensitive data must be appropriately protected (encryption, pseudonymisation where relevant). 4.2 Health-data hosting (HDS). The infrastructure hosting The solution must hold the French Hébergeur de Données de Santé (HDS) certification. 4.3 Explainability and traceability. Recommendations or suggestions produced by The solution must be explainable. It must be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements that led to an output (source grounding, audit trail), consistent with HAS guidance on the use of AI in healthcare. 4.4 Medical responsibility." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk50> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client's global budget is 900,000 over 5 years, with an annual operating cost that must remain controlled and compatible with the authority's budgetary capacity. Given our pricing model and current financial position, what is our projected margin on this contract, and are there cost-optimisation strategies our can propose? our target gross margin percentage ranges from 25% to 35%." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk51> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client's global budget matches our reference budget for similar projects. To determine our projected margin on this contract, our first need to consider the cost structure, which includes one-off project costs and recurring run costs. our budget envelope indicates that one-off project costs typically account for 30% of the total budget, while recurring run costs make up 70%." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk52> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For a €900,000 budget over 5 years, this would translate to approximately €270,000 in one-off project costs and €630,000 in recurring costs. Given our target gross margin range, our aim to maintain a balance between cost efficiency and service quality. our standard daily rates for various roles can help our estimate the personnel costs involved in delivering the project." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk53> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, without specific details on the project requirements and the exact makeup of the team needed, it's challenging to provide an precise margin projection. That said, assuming our can efficiently allocate resources and manage costs within our target gross margin range, a potential projected margin could be between 25% and 35% of the total contract value. a potential projected margin would put a potential projected margin in the range of €225,000 to €315,000 over the 5-year period." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk54> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As for cost-optimisation strategies, our can propose several approaches based on our commercial posture, which favours configurations that protect gross margins and recurring-cost predictability. our could suggest: 1. **Optimising Hosting and Inference Costs**: our note on cost structure indicates that hosting and inference costs vary materially with the hosting tier and model option selected. Choosing more cost-efficient tiers or models without compromising performance could help reduce recurring run costs. 2. **Efficient Project Framing and Design**: Ensuring that one-off project costs such as framing, design, integration, change management, and training are efficiently managed and do not exceed the allocated 30% of the budget can also contribute to cost savings. 3. **Leveraging our Financial Capacity**: With a comfortable cash runway following our Series A funding, our have the financial flexibility to invest in the project's initial phases, potentially leading to more efficient and cost-effective solutions in the long run. 4. **Adopting a Cost-Efficient Pricing Model**: our can work with the client to identify areas where our standard daily rates might be adjusted based on the specific needs of the project, ensuring that both parties achieve both parties objectives without unnecessary expenditure." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk55> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By focusing on these strategies and maintaining a disciplined approach to cost management, our can aim to achieve a margin within our target range while delivering value to the client." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk56> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires a solution that provides intelligent assistance tools, facilitates access to information, improves the quality of written outputs, and reduces processing and documentation times." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk57> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What AI components and innovation strategy will we use to deliver a solution that provides intelligent assistance tools, facilitates access to information, improves the quality of written outputs, and reduces processing and documentation times, and how will we ensure a solution that provides intelligent assistance tools, facilitates access to information, improves the quality of written outputs, and reduces processing and documentation times meets The client requirements?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk58> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To address the client's requirements, we will leverage we core approach of Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) which generates answers from passages retrieved from The client controlled corpus. we ai_llm_rag_capabilities include hybrid retrieval, re-ranking, query reformulation, multi-document synthesis, structured extraction, template-guided drafting, and applicable rules recall during dossier handling. we will employ we capabilities to assist with drafting clinical and administrative content, provide contextualized answers, and surface relevant information to staff members. we solution will be designed to fit into existing practices without introducing a rupture in clinical or administrative workflows, ensuring that the intelligent assistance tool is accessible from the hospital staff's work environment. we innovation strategy involves an iterative approach, including corpus selection and curation with The client experts, retrieval tuning, prompt and template design per use case, and evaluation loop. we will measure answer quality using a labelled evaluation set built with the client, focusing on groundedness, relevance, and factual support." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk59> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure we solution meets the client's requirements, we will provide explainability features such as source citations, retrieved passages, retrieval trace, and logging of every interaction for posterior audit. we solution will also be designed to preserve medical confidentiality, protect sensitive data, and ensure data sovereignty. we will work closely with the client to define data use terms and ensure that we solution complies with regulatory requirements. we will select a suitable model option from we available models, considering factors such as performance, explainability, and sovereignty. we Sovereign European open-weight model is fully auditable and well-suited for explainability-driven and sovereignty-driven requirements, while we top-tier proprietary models offer higher performance on complex drafting and reasoning tasks." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk6> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must be designed as an assistance tool. No clinical or medico-administrative decision may be automated without explicit validation by a qualified professional. The solution must be positioned so as not to require medical-device qualification (CE marking / MDR); should any use case approach medical-device qualification (CE marking / MDR), the bidder must explicitly address the implications. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance. The solution must provide response times compatible with daily clinical use." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk60> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By leveraging we AI capabilities, innovation strategy, and commitment to explainability, data sovereignty, and regulatory compliance, we are confident that we solution will meet The client requirements and provide a valuable intelligent assistance tool for hospital staff." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk61> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client wishes to limit the environmental footprint of The client information systems and requires a solution that contributes to reducing energy consumption and relies on low-carbon infrastructure." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk62> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What sustainability measures will we implement to meet these requirements, and how will we ensure we solution is environmentally responsible?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk63> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As a CSR & Sustainability officer at we, I can confirm that we have already implemented various environmental capabilities to reduce we footprint. we partner with green hosting providers like OuraneCloud, which uses renewable energy and has a power usage effectiveness (PUE) of 1.2, indicating efficient energy use." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk64> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, OuraneCloud, which uses renewable energy and has a power usage effectiveness (PUE) of 1.2, indicating efficient energy use reuses heat, further minimizing waste.  we also practice digital sobriety through model right-sizing, caching, and batching, which helps reduce the computational resources required for we operations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk65> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Moreover, we have a carbon reporting capability that allows we to track and manage we carbon footprint effectively." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk66> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To address The client specific requirements, we will ensure that our solution relies on low-carbon infrastructure, such as OuraneCloud, which uses renewable energy and has a power usage effectiveness (PUE) of 1.2, indicating efficient energy use, and optimizes energy consumption through we digital sobriety practices. we will also provide regular carbon footprint reports to demonstrate we commitment to reducing energy consumption and minimizing our environmental impact." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk67> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Furthermore, as part of we csr profile, we have a published trajectory to reduce carbon intensity per managed assistant year on year, indicating we long-term commitment to sustainability." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk68> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By implementing these measures, we can ensure that our solution is environmentally responsible and contributes to reducing The client environmental footprint." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk69> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) can rely on The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) consortium to design, implement, and deploy an artificial intelligence solution that assists hospital staff in hospital staff daily activities, improving efficiency and quality of care while ensuring strict compliance with regulatory requirements. The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) project plan, based on a hybrid delivery model combining agile iterations with a phase-gate structure, consists of five phases: Framing, Design, Pilot, Generalisation, and Run. Framing will last approximately 2-3 months, during which The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) will work closely with the client to define the project scope, objectives, and deliverables." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk7> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As an indication, a response time below 2 seconds is expected for common queries. A high level of answer relevance is expected. 5.2 Availability. Continuity of care requires a high level of availability, including outside office hours (24/7 services). An availability target of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration and interoperability. The solution must integrate with the existing hospital information system (SIH) and the electronic patient record (DPI)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk70> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Design will focus on designing the solution, including the development of the intelligent assistance tool and integration with existing hospital information systems, and is expected to take around 4-5 months. Pilot will involve deploying the solution on a limited perimeter, testing, and validating the solution effectiveness, and The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) anticipate Pilot to last about 3-4 months. Following the successful completion of Pilot, The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) will proceed with Generalisatione Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB), expected to take around 6-8 months." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk71> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Finally, in Run, The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) will ensure the smooth operation of the solution, provide maintenance and support, and continue to monitor and improve the solution performance. the solution will provide hospital staff with an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from hospital staff work environment, capable of supporting hospital staff in hospital staff clinical-administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of supporting them in their clinical-administrative activities will facilitate access to information, improve the quality of written outputs, and reduce processing and documentation times. The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) will achieve this through The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) core approach of Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), which generates answers from passages retrieved from the client's controlled corpus. the solution must fit into the existing practices of staff and must not introduce a rupture in clinical or administrative workflows. The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) ai_llm_rag_capabilities include hybrid retrieval, re-ranking, query reformulation, multi-document synthesis, structured extraction, template-guided drafting, and applicable rules recall during dossier handling." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk72> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) will employ Our ai_llm_rag_capabilities to assist with drafting clinical and administrative content, provide contextualized answers, and surface relevant information to staff members. The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) are committed to ensuring the solution meets the client's requirements for response times below 2 seconds, although The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) current technology stack only partially covers meets, with a median latency of 1.3 seconds and common single-document queries below 2 seconds at p95. However, complex multi-source synthesis queries may reach up to 2.5 seconds at p95." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk73> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) will explore optimizing The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) platform's configuration or scaling up The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) infrastructure to ensure that complex multi-source synthesis queries can be completed within the 2-second threshold. the solution will integrate with the existing hospital information system (SIH) and electronic patient record (DPI), supporting health interoperability standards such as HL7 and FHIR, with a production-grade FHIR-HL7 connector for the main resources and extended resource coverage on the roadmap. The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) will provide API-type interfaces for easy integration with existing hospital information systems and electronic patient records. The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) take data sovereignty seriously and will host the solution on SecNumCloud-qualified infrastructure or equivalent, such as OuraneCloud, which is a sovereign cloud that ensures data is hosted exclusively within the European Union." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk74> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) will also ensure that sensitive data is protected through encryption, pseudonymisation, and strict key management practices. The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) maintains regulatory compliance with the help of The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) Security & Compliance function, particularly in the context of health deployment. The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) monitor obligations related to GDPR, including Art. 9 special-category data and Art. 28 processing agreements, medical confidentiality, HDS framework, and EU AI Act requirements. the solution will be designed as an assistance tool, and no clinical or medico-administrative decision may be automated without explicit validation by a qualified professional." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk75> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at €900,000 over 5 years, which matches The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) reference budget for similar projects. The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) aim to maintain a balance between cost efficiency and service quality, with a target gross margin percentage ranging from 25% to 35%. The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) will propose an approach that optimises costs while guaranteeing the expected quality of service." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk76> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As part of The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) csr profile, The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) have implemented various environmental capabilities to reduce The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) footprint. The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) partner with green hosting providers like OuraneCloud, which uses renewable energy and has a power usage effectiveness (PUE) of 1.2, indicating efficient energy use. The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) also practice digital sobriety through model right-sizing, caching, and batching, which helps reduce the computational resources required for The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) operations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk77> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) will ensure that the solution relies on low-carbon infrastructure, such as OuraneCloud, and optimizes energy consumption through The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) digital sobriety practices. The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) will provide regular carbon footprint reports to demonstrate The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) commitment to reducing energy consumption and minimizing our environmental impact. By implementing these measures, The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) can ensure that the solution is environmentally responsible and contributes to reducing the client's environmental footprint." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk78> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In conclusion, The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) is confident that the solution meets the client's requirements for an artificial intelligence assistance tool that improves efficiency and quality of care while ensuring strict compliance with regulatory requirements. The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) look forward to working closely with the client's to deliver a successful project that benefits hospital staff and patients alike." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk8> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must support health interoperability standards (HL7 / FHIR), the national health identifier (INS), and the national framework (Ségur du numérique en santé, Mon espace santé / DMP). API-type interfaces are expected, as is integration with user directories. 6. Sovereignty constraints the authority's attaches particular importance to data sovereignty. Hosting must be performed on SecNumCloud-qualified infrastructure or equivalent, and particular attention will be paid to dependency on non-European suppliers. 7. Budget constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 900,000 over 5 years." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk9> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The annual operating cost must remain controlled and compatible with the authority's budgetary capacity. The titleholder must propose an approach that optimises costs while guaranteeing the expected quality of service. 8. Environmental constraints As part of the authority's sustainable-development policy, the authority's wishes to limit the environmental footprint of the authority's information systems. The titleholder must propose a solution that contributes to reducing energy consumption and relies, as far as possible, on low-carbon infrastructure. 9. Deployment terms the project must be conducted progressively, with a pilot phase on a limited perimeter (one or two departments) followed by progressive generalisation to all services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

